to is doing the same for  many something more meaningful is  happening off the ice than on  550 health care workers fully vaccinated  attending the game  in person a way of thanking frontline  workers for their courage and hard work  during the pandemic  and a sign that life in this country is  getting back to normal and patel is a  nurse  and thrilled that health care workers  were picked to be in the stands  absolutely and we were all of us want  that because we are tired of this  pandemic the healthcare workers deserve  it i mean they've  what they've been through this last year  and changed it's uh it's unlike anything  we've ever seen as thoughts turn to the  game the two canadian teams with the  longest history will engineer one more  memorable outcome for montreal a win  would be a sweet surprise  for toronto an end to a legacy of  playoff failure  a loss for the leafs could change the  fortunes for everyone from management to  the coaches to the players  this game is probably the most important  franchise  game in the last several decades but for  leafs fans this is no time for pessimism  it's game seven game sevens are always  unique so long as uh  we play a good game i mean you can't  really ask for more well the leafs could  ask to win a playoff series for a change  eric sorensen global news toronto and  that is global national for this monday  i'm donna friesen tonight's here at  canada is island lake  in alberta thanks for watching hope to  see you here again tomorrow  bye
 

